# Network proxy (Clash Verge)

Owner machine runs **Clash Verge** (Mihomo). When `git push` / `git pull` to GitHub fails with `443 Connection was reset` or `Could not connect`, use this proxy for that shell session only — do **not** permanently rewrite `git config`.

- **HTTP/HTTPS/mixed**: `http://127.0.0.1:7890`
- **App**: Clash Verge · system proxy `127.0.0.1:7890` · mixed port `7890`
- **OS**: Windows 11

## How to push

```powershell
$env:HTTP_PROXY = "http://127.0.0.1:7890"
$env:HTTPS_PROXY = "http://127.0.0.1:7890"
$env:ALL_PROXY = "http://127.0.0.1:7890"
git push origin HEAD
```

If Clash is off or push still fails: keep using **b64 VPS short commands** (no GitHub pull required). Do not print or commit proxy credentials (none here — local only).
